<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 110 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 110 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 110 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			   EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    600 MLN    600 MLN    600 MLN    600 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    200 MLN    500 MLN    610 MLN</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    200 MLN*   300 MLN*   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE	    =	    =	    110 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
